.TH CHTTPCLI_SET_ENGINE_NUM_REACTOR_THREADS 3 "2026-07-17" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpcli_set_engine_num_reactor_threads \- set the OS thread count of the async engine reactor of chttpclient
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpclient.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpcli_set_engine_num_reactor_threads(size_t num_threads);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function sets how many OS threads the async engine's shared
ccol_event_loop reactor (the one behind Tier 2 and Tier 3) uses for
polling and dispatch. The rules of the num_reactor_threads parameter
of ccol_event_loop_create_mp apply (see cthreadcomm.h): 1 means a
single thread that both polls and dispatches inline, and a larger
value means one dedicated poller thread plus (num_threads - 1)
dispatch worker threads.

By default the reactor sizes itself to sysconf(_SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN),
or to 1 if that query fails. You get this default when you never call
the function, and also when you call it with num_threads == 0. A
positive num_threads replaces the automatic size and pins the reactor
to exactly that many threads, and a num_threads of 0 brings the
automatic size back. The setting only affects how the shared reactor
is built and has nothing to do with the settings of any single
chttpcli instance.

You can call this function at only two points: before the reactor
first starts in this process (before the first call to
chttpclient_do_async or chttpclient_do_async_streaming anywhere), or
after the engine has stopped completely. The engine stops once every
async user of a chttpcli has dropped its reference and the automatic
teardown has finished, and chttpcli_engine_wait blocks until that
teardown is over. The reactor behind
chttpsvr_set_engine_num_reactor_threads usually lives as long as the
process, but this engine starts and stops along with the Tier 2
and Tier 3 traffic, so the window for this call opens again every time
the engine stops and is not a one-time chance at process start.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success, if the call succeeds.
ccol_not_permitted, while the engine runs. Wait for the engine to stop
    completely first.
.fi
